From: Dindin Suryadi <din2.suryadi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:48:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Disable ColorFade EGL animation on MT8127

Mali-450 shim_eglMakeCurrent crashes inside system_server (SIGSEGV at
0x14) when ColorFade prepares/detaches its GL context on screen off,
causing a soft-reboot instead of turning off HDMI via hdmi_power_daemon.
Returning false from ColorFade.prepare() skips the GL fade animation and
lets DisplayPowerController transition cleanly to Display.STATE_OFF.

---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/display/ColorFade.java
@@ -137,6 +137,11 @@ final class ColorFade {
      * @return True if the color fade is ready, false if it is uncontrollable.
      */
     public boolean prepare(Context context, int mode) {
+        // Skip EGL ColorFade on MT8127 Mali-450 to avoid system_server SIGSEGV on sleep.
+        if (android.os.SystemProperties.getBoolean("persist.sys.disable_colorfade", true)) {
+            return false;
+        }
+
         if (DEBUG) {
             Slog.d(TAG, "prepare: mode=" + mode);
         }
